§§ `Article 26 — Loans from the cash value`
-- src:1182 | ĐIỀU 26 : TẠM ỨNG TỪ GIÁ TRỊ TIỀN MẶT

-- 26.1: while the contract is in force the policyholder may borrow from the cash value if
-- (i) the contract has one and (ii) all loans, past unrepaid, present, and unpaid interest,
-- come to no more than 80% of the cash value at the request and no less than the Company's
-- minimum. 26.2 to 26.4: the rate and the minimum repayment are the Company's to publish.
